    <item>
      <title>Exploring Helsinki Through the Dreamy Architecture of Eliel Saarinen</title>
      <link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/07/31/travel/helsinki-architecture-eliel-saarinen-art-nouveau.html</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/07/31/travel/helsinki-architecture-eliel-saarinen-art-nouveau.html</guid>
      <atom:link href="https://www.nytimes.com/2026/07/31/travel/helsinki-architecture-eliel-saarinen-art-nouveau.html" rel="standout"></atom:link>
      <description>A writer goes in search of the architect Eliel Saarinen, whose Art Nouveau-inspired designs helped shape early-1900s Finland as well as midcentury America.</description>
      <dc:creator>Michael H. Hodges and Vesa Laitinen</dc:creator>
      <pubDate>Fri, 31 Jul 2026 09:03:02 +0000</pubDate>
      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_per">Saarinen, Eliel</category>
      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_geo">Helsinki (Finland)</category>
      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/des">Travel and Vacations</category>
      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/des">Architecture</category>
      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/des">Historic Buildings and Sites</category>
      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/des">Content Type: Personal Profile</category>
      <media:content height="1801" medium="image" url="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/07/31/multimedia/31trav-helsinki-saarinen-jcgv/31trav-helsinki-saarinen-jcgv-mediumSquareAt3X.jpg" width="1800"></media:content>
      <media:description>The Pohjola Insurance headquarters, in Helsinki, exemplifies Eliel Saarinen’s early work. Its decorations — foxes, bears and grinning figures — draw from Finland’s founding epic, the “Kalevala.”</media:description>
    </item>
